IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dog-act-domain`

-- =============================================================================
-- Dog Act 1976 (Western Australia) -- Part XI, Transitional provisions
--
-- Isomorphic encoding of ss 55-65, as at the compilation dated 28 Nov 2024
-- [version 08-b0-00], re-verified current 2026-09-09. Source:
-- mrdoc_47983.txt (WA compilation bundle), lines 1824-1893.
--
-- This Part is, on its face, "largely spent/historical transitional
-- machinery" (per the assignment brief), and the read confirms that
-- honestly: every section is either (a) a savings clause with no computed
-- content, (b) a deeming/grandfathering rule bridging an old regime to a
-- new one for facts fixed at a past commencement day, or (c) a bare
-- administrative discretion with no fact a downstream rule would test.
-- NONE of ss 55-65 creates an offence with a Penalty, and NONE imposes a
-- "must do X within N days" duty on a named actor with breach consequences
-- -- s. 60(3)'s 12-month regulation-making cutoff is a VALIDITY window on a
-- rule-making power, not a party's obligation, so it is encoded the way
-- this corpus already encodes such cutoffs (s. 33F(3)'s day-count style in
-- dog-act-1976.l4), not as a PARTY/MUST/WITHIN rule. Accordingly this file
-- contains no regulative rules and no #TRACE.
--
-- SCOPED OUT (cited at their site with a trailing "-- @ref ... scoped out,
-- fact-supplied" comment, never expanded): s. 8 and s. 8(1) as inserted by
-- the Dog Amendment Act 2013 s. 7 (assistance dogs), s. 16 (registration
-- procedure, read by both s. 57 and s. 64), s. 29(1) (authorised-persons
-- appointment, read by s. 61) and s. 29(3) (seizure/detention, read by
-- s. 58), s. 33E(1) and s. 33F(1) (dangerous-dog declarations and notices
-- -- already encoded in dog-act-1976.l4, but NOT imported here per the
-- assignment's instruction to treat cross-references back into that
-- material as external inputs), Local Government Act 1995 s. 9.10(2) (a
-- different Act entirely), and ss 38A, 38B, 38G-38L, 38N (pet shop
-- provisions -- outside this chunk's assigned line range, being encoded
-- elsewhere in this same effort).
-- =============================================================================

§ `Part XI -- Transitional provisions`

-- [Heading inserted: No. 18 of 2013 s. 59.]

§§ `Division 1 -- Transitional provisions for the Dog Amendment Act 2013`

-- [Heading inserted: No. 18 of 2013 s. 59; amended: No. 16 of 2019 s. 110.]

§§§ `55. Application of Interpretation Act 1984`

-- s 55 is a pure savings clause: "The provisions of this Division do not
-- prejudice or affect the application of the Interpretation Act 1984 to
-- and in relation to the repeals ... effected by the Dog Amendment Act
-- 2013." There is no fact this encoding derives from a savings clause of
-- this shape -- it disclaims an effect on a DIFFERENT Act's application,
-- rather than stating a rule of its own -- so, following the s 33D(3)
-- precedent in dog-act-1976.l4, it is recorded here as inert prose and not
-- force-fit into a boolean.

§§§ `56. Authorisations in relation to assistance dogs`

DECLARE `S56 Facts` HAS
    `dog was specified in an authority given by the Minister under old s 8`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `that authority was in effect immediately before the s 7 commencement day`          IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 8, s. 8(1) as inserted by Dog Amendment Act 2013 s. 7 -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 56 (transitional; Dog Amendment Act 2013 s. 59)
GIVEN f IS A `S56 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56 -- the dog is taken to be an assistance dog` f MEANS
        f's `dog was specified in an authority given by the Minister under old s 8`
    AND f's `that authority was in effect immediately before the s 7 commencement day`

§§§ `57. Registration procedure`

DECLARE `S57 Facts` HAS
    `application for registration was delivered under old s 16(1)`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `application was not finally dealt with under old s 16(2) before the s 14 commencement day`      IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16 -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 57 (transitional; Dog Amendment Act 2013 s. 59)
GIVEN f IS A `S57 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57 -- the application is to be dealt with under the pre-2013 s 16 procedure` f MEANS
        f's `application for registration was delivered under old s 16(1)`
    AND f's `application was not finally dealt with under old s 16(2) before the s 14 commencement day`

§§§ `58. Detained dogs`

DECLARE `S58 Facts` HAS
    `dog was being detained by or on behalf of a local government immediately before the s 25 commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog had been seized under s 29(3)`                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 29(3) -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 58 (transitional; Dog Amendment Act 2013 s. 59)
GIVEN f IS A `S58 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58 -- the dog continues to be dealt with under the pre-2013 seizure and detention regime` f MEANS
        f's `dog was being detained by or on behalf of a local government immediately before the s 25 commencement day`
    AND f's `dog had been seized under s 29(3)`

§§§ `59. Dogs declared to be dangerous dogs`

DECLARE `S59 Facts` HAS
    `a declaration under s 33E(1) was in effect immediately before the s 34 commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 33E(1), s. 33F(1) -- scoped out, fact-supplied (encoded in dog-act-1976.l4; not imported here per assignment)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 59, first limb (transitional; Dog Amendment Act 2013 s. 59)
GIVEN f IS A `S59 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 59 -- the declaration continues as a declaration under the amended s 33E(1)` f MEANS
    f's `a declaration under s 33E(1) was in effect immediately before the s 34 commencement day`

-- s 59's second limb ("but any order imposed by the notice given under ...
-- s 33F(1) ceases to have effect") is an unconditional consequence of the
-- same antecedent fact, not a separately-conditioned rule -- so it shares
-- the one Facts record above rather than inventing a second antecedent.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 59, second limb (transitional; Dog Amendment Act 2013 s. 59)
GIVEN f IS A `S59 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 59 -- any order imposed by the s 33F(1) notice ceases to have effect` f MEANS
    f's `a declaration under s 33E(1) was in effect immediately before the s 34 commencement day`

§§§ `60. Transitional regulations`

-- s 60(1)'s definitions (commencement day -- two cases, Gazettal day,
-- transitional matter, transitional regulations) are folded directly into
-- the parameter/field names below rather than separately DECLAREd, since
-- none of them is read anywhere else in this Part.

-- s 60(2): a discretionary regulation-making POWER ("Regulations may
-- prescribe anything else required, necessary or convenient ... in
-- connection with" the 2013 Act's enactment or a later amending
-- provision) -- not a party's obligation, and no fact a downstream rule in
-- this file tests beyond what s 60(3)-(5) already capture (those sections
-- test properties of regulations made under this power -- their timing,
-- their retrospective terms, their limits -- not whether the power itself
-- was exercised). Recorded as inert prose, on the same footing as s 62(2)
-- below.

DECLARE `S60(3) Facts` HAS
    `months elapsed since commencement day` IS A NUMBER
        -- unit is MONTHS, matching the statute's own "period of 12 months" (this file's
        -- day-count sibling sections use DAYS; each function documents its own unit)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 60(3)
GIVEN f IS A `S60(3) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(3) -- transitional regulations may still be made` f MEANS
    f's `months elapsed since commencement day` AT MOST 12

DECLARE `S60(4) Facts` HAS
    `the regulations provide the state of affairs existed from an operative day earlier than Gazettal day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `operative day, as an offset in days from commencement day (0 = commencement day, negative = earlier)` IS A NUMBER

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 60(4)
GIVEN f IS A `S60(4) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(4) -- the retrospective transitional regulation has effect according to its terms` f MEANS
        f's `the regulations provide the state of affairs existed from an operative day earlier than Gazettal day`
    AND f's `operative day, as an offset in days from commencement day (0 = commencement day, negative = earlier)` AT LEAST 0

DECLARE `S60(5) Facts` HAS
    `person is the State or an authority of the State`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `provision would prejudicially affect this person's rights existing before Gazettal day`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `provision would impose a liability on this person for something done or omitted before Gazettal day` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 60(5)
GIVEN f IS A `S60(5) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(5) -- the s 60(4) retrospective provision does not overreach against this person` f MEANS
        f's `person is the State or an authority of the State`
    OR  NOT (   f's `provision would prejudicially affect this person's rights existing before Gazettal day`
             OR f's `provision would impose a liability on this person for something done or omitted before Gazettal day`)

§§ `Division 2 -- Transitional provision for the Local Government Legislation Amendment Act 2019`

-- [Heading inserted: No. 16 of 2019 s. 111.]

§§§ `61. Authorised persons`

DECLARE `S61 Facts` HAS
    `person was appointed under old s 29(1) immediately before the s 109 commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 29(1) -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 61
GIVEN f IS A `S61 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 61 -- the person is taken to be an authorised person under Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2)` f MEANS
    f's `person was appointed under old s 29(1) immediately before the s 109 commencement day`
        -- @ref Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s. 9.10(2) -- scoped out, fact-supplied (a different Act)

§§ `Division 3 -- Transitional provisions for the Dog Amendment (Stop Puppy Farming) Act 2021`

-- [Heading inserted: No. 29 of 2021 s. 44.]

§§§ `62. Transitional provision for centralised registration system`

-- s 62(2): a purely discretionary administrative power -- the CEO MAY
-- establish and maintain the centralised registration system before the
-- commencement day, and MAY permit local governments to record information
-- in it or transfer information into it. There is no numeric WITHIN period
-- ("before the commencement day" is an open-ended, moving-target
-- eventuality, not a fixed N from a reference point in this file) and no
-- fact a downstream rule would test beyond what s 62(3) already captures.
-- Following the assignment's own example ("the CEO must establish a
-- database"), this is recorded as inert prose rather than a force-fit
-- boolean or a MAY rule with an invented deadline.

DECLARE `S62(3) Facts` HAS
    `information was recorded by a local government in the centralised system under s 62(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `information was transferred to the centralised system under s 62(2)(b)`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the recording or transfer occurred before the commencement day`                              IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 62(3)
GIVEN f IS A `S62(3) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 62(3) -- the information is taken to be information recorded by the local government on its own register` f MEANS
        (f's `information was recorded by a local government in the centralised system under s 62(2)(a)`
         OR f's `information was transferred to the centralised system under s 62(2)(b)`)
    AND f's `the recording or transfer occurred before the commencement day`

§§§ `63. Registered unsterilised dogs`

DECLARE `S63 Facts` HAS
    `the dog is not sterilised`                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dog's registration was, immediately before the s 16 commencement day, in effect under old s 15` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 63(2)
GIVEN f IS A `S63 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63 -- the pre-2021 s 15 registration regime continues to apply to this registration` f MEANS
        f's `the dog is not sterilised`
    AND f's `the dog's registration was, immediately before the s 16 commencement day, in effect under old s 15`

§§§ `64. Application for registration`

DECLARE `S64 Facts` HAS
    `application for registration was delivered under s 16(1)`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `application was not finally dealt with under s 16(2) before the s 17 commencement day`         IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16 -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 64
GIVEN f IS A `S64 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64 -- the application is to be dealt with as if s 17(5) had not been enacted` f MEANS
        f's `application for registration was delivered under s 16(1)`
    AND f's `application was not finally dealt with under s 16(2) before the s 17 commencement day`

§§§ `65. Transition period for relevant pet shop businesses`

-- "application day" (s 65(1)) is "the prescribed date" -- a value fixed by
-- regulations, outside this chunk's assigned range -- and "preexisting
-- dog"/"relevant pet shop business" cross-refer to s 38A, also outside this
-- chunk. Both are treated as fact-supplied inputs below rather than
-- expanded.

DECLARE `S65(2)(a) Facts` HAS
    `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `time is before the application day`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 65(1) "application day" (the prescribed date) -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 65(2)(a)
GIVEN f IS A `S65(2)(a) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(2)(a) -- ss 38B, 38G, 38H, 38I, 38J, 38K and 38L do not apply to the person's pet shop business or pet shop` f MEANS
        f's `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day`
    AND f's `time is before the application day`
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss. 38B, 38G, 38H, 38I, 38J, 38K, 38L -- scoped out, fact-supplied (outside assigned range)

DECLARE `S65(2)(b) Facts` HAS
    `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dog is a preexisting dog (supplied to the business before the application day)`         IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 65(1) "preexisting dog", s. 38A -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 65(2)(b)
GIVEN f IS A `S65(2)(b) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(2)(b) -- ss 38G, 38I, 38J, 38K and 38L do not apply to the person in relation to this dog` f MEANS
        f's `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day`
    AND f's `the dog is a preexisting dog (supplied to the business before the application day)`
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss. 38G, 38I, 38J, 38K, 38L -- scoped out, fact-supplied (outside assigned range)
        -- note: unlike (2)(a), this limb carries no "before the application day" cutoff of
        -- its own in the source text -- the exemption for a given preexisting dog is not
        -- time-limited by (2)'s chapeau beyond fixing which dogs qualify as "preexisting"

-- AMBIGUITY (F-S65-3-PERSON-SCOPE): "the person" in s 65(3) is not textually tied back to
-- the "a person [who] conducts a relevant pet shop business" of s 65(2)'s chapeau by its
-- own words -- (3) reads as a bare, seemingly unconditional sentence ("Section 38N does
-- not apply to a person before the application day"). Taken reading: (3) is part of the
-- same transitional scheme as (2), and "the person" picks up the same antecedent (a
-- person conducting a relevant pet shop business immediately before the commencement
-- day) -- because a "Transition period for relevant pet shop businesses" section
-- granting an exemption to literally any person in Western Australia, regardless of
-- whether they run such a business, would be an absurd reading of a section whose whole
-- subject is that business. Rejected: an unconditional exemption reaching any person
-- whatsoever, unlinked to (2)'s antecedent. Recorded as ambiguity
-- F-S65-3-PERSON-SCOPE in this chunk's returned ambiguity register.
DECLARE `S65(3) Facts` HAS
    `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `time is before the application day`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 65(3)
GIVEN f IS A `S65(3) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(3) -- s 38N does not apply to the person` f MEANS
        f's `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day`
    AND f's `time is before the application day`
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38N -- scoped out, fact-supplied (outside assigned range)

-- =============================================================================
-- Illustrations
-- =============================================================================

§ `Illustrations`

`s 56 -- an authorised assistance dog` MEANS `S56 Facts` WITH
    `dog was specified in an authority given by the Minister under old s 8` IS TRUE
    , `that authority was in effect immediately before the s 7 commencement day` IS TRUE

`s 56 -- an authority that had already lapsed` MEANS `S56 Facts` WITH
    `dog was specified in an authority given by the Minister under old s 8` IS TRUE
    , `that authority was in effect immediately before the s 7 commencement day` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 56 -- the dog is taken to be an assistance dog` `s 56 -- an authorised assistance dog`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 56 -- the dog is taken to be an assistance dog` `s 56 -- an authority that had already lapsed`)

`s 57 -- a pending application` MEANS `S57 Facts` WITH
    `application for registration was delivered under old s 16(1)` IS TRUE
    , `application was not finally dealt with under old s 16(2) before the s 14 commencement day` IS TRUE

`s 57 -- an application already finally dealt with` MEANS `S57 Facts` WITH
    `application for registration was delivered under old s 16(1)` IS TRUE
    , `application was not finally dealt with under old s 16(2) before the s 14 commencement day` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 57 -- the application is to be dealt with under the pre-2013 s 16 procedure` `s 57 -- a pending application`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57 -- the application is to be dealt with under the pre-2013 s 16 procedure` `s 57 -- an application already finally dealt with`)

`s 58 -- a dog detained under the old regime at commencement` MEANS `S58 Facts` WITH
    `dog was being detained by or on behalf of a local government immediately before the s 25 commencement day` IS TRUE
    , `dog had been seized under s 29(3)` IS TRUE

`s 58 -- a dog not seized under s 29(3)` MEANS `S58 Facts` WITH
    `dog was being detained by or on behalf of a local government immediately before the s 25 commencement day` IS TRUE
    , `dog had been seized under s 29(3)` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 58 -- the dog continues to be dealt with under the pre-2013 seizure and detention regime` `s 58 -- a dog detained under the old regime at commencement`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 58 -- the dog continues to be dealt with under the pre-2013 seizure and detention regime` `s 58 -- a dog not seized under s 29(3)`)

`s 59 -- a declaration in effect at commencement` MEANS `S59 Facts` WITH
    `a declaration under s 33E(1) was in effect immediately before the s 34 commencement day` IS TRUE

`s 59 -- no declaration was in effect` MEANS `S59 Facts` WITH
    `a declaration under s 33E(1) was in effect immediately before the s 34 commencement day` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 59 -- the declaration continues as a declaration under the amended s 33E(1)` `s 59 -- a declaration in effect at commencement`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 59 -- the declaration continues as a declaration under the amended s 33E(1)` `s 59 -- no declaration was in effect`)
#ASSERT `s 59 -- any order imposed by the s 33F(1) notice ceases to have effect` `s 59 -- a declaration in effect at commencement`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 59 -- any order imposed by the s 33F(1) notice ceases to have effect` `s 59 -- no declaration was in effect`)

`s 60(3) -- within the 12-month window` MEANS `S60(3) Facts` WITH `months elapsed since commencement day` IS 12
`s 60(3) -- past the 12-month window` MEANS `S60(3) Facts` WITH `months elapsed since commencement day` IS 13

#ASSERT `s 60(3) -- transitional regulations may still be made` `s 60(3) -- within the 12-month window`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 60(3) -- transitional regulations may still be made` `s 60(3) -- past the 12-month window`)

`s 60(4) -- operative day not earlier than commencement day` MEANS `S60(4) Facts` WITH
    `the regulations provide the state of affairs existed from an operative day earlier than Gazettal day` IS TRUE
    , `operative day, as an offset in days from commencement day (0 = commencement day, negative = earlier)` IS 5

`s 60(4) -- operative day earlier than commencement day` MEANS `S60(4) Facts` WITH
    `the regulations provide the state of affairs existed from an operative day earlier than Gazettal day` IS TRUE
    , `operative day, as an offset in days from commencement day (0 = commencement day, negative = earlier)` IS -5

#ASSERT `s 60(4) -- the retrospective transitional regulation has effect according to its terms` `s 60(4) -- operative day not earlier than commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 60(4) -- the retrospective transitional regulation has effect according to its terms` `s 60(4) -- operative day earlier than commencement day`)

`s 60(5) -- an ordinary person whose pre-Gazettal rights would be prejudiced` MEANS `S60(5) Facts` WITH
    `person is the State or an authority of the State` IS FALSE
    , `provision would prejudicially affect this person's rights existing before Gazettal day` IS TRUE
    , `provision would impose a liability on this person for something done or omitted before Gazettal day` IS FALSE

`s 60(5) -- the State itself, whose pre-Gazettal rights would be affected` MEANS `S60(5) Facts` WITH
    `person is the State or an authority of the State` IS TRUE
    , `provision would prejudicially affect this person's rights existing before Gazettal day` IS TRUE
    , `provision would impose a liability on this person for something done or omitted before Gazettal day` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`s 60(5) -- the s 60(4) retrospective provision does not overreach against this person` `s 60(5) -- an ordinary person whose pre-Gazettal rights would be prejudiced`)
#ASSERT `s 60(5) -- the s 60(4) retrospective provision does not overreach against this person` `s 60(5) -- the State itself, whose pre-Gazettal rights would be affected`

`s 61 -- a serving s 29(1) appointee at commencement` MEANS `S61 Facts` WITH
    `person was appointed under old s 29(1) immediately before the s 109 commencement day` IS TRUE

`s 61 -- no s 29(1) appointment held at commencement` MEANS `S61 Facts` WITH
    `person was appointed under old s 29(1) immediately before the s 109 commencement day` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 61 -- the person is taken to be an authorised person under Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2)` `s 61 -- a serving s 29(1) appointee at commencement`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 61 -- the person is taken to be an authorised person under Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2)` `s 61 -- no s 29(1) appointment held at commencement`)

`s 62(3) -- information recorded pre-commencement under s 62(2)(a)` MEANS `S62(3) Facts` WITH
    `information was recorded by a local government in the centralised system under s 62(2)(a)` IS TRUE
    , `information was transferred to the centralised system under s 62(2)(b)` IS FALSE
    , `the recording or transfer occurred before the commencement day` IS TRUE

`s 62(3) -- information recorded after commencement day` MEANS `S62(3) Facts` WITH
    `information was recorded by a local government in the centralised system under s 62(2)(a)` IS TRUE
    , `information was transferred to the centralised system under s 62(2)(b)` IS FALSE
    , `the recording or transfer occurred before the commencement day` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 62(3) -- the information is taken to be information recorded by the local government on its own register` `s 62(3) -- information recorded pre-commencement under s 62(2)(a)`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 62(3) -- the information is taken to be information recorded by the local government on its own register` `s 62(3) -- information recorded after commencement day`)

`s 63 -- an unsterilised dog registered under old s 15 at commencement` MEANS `S63 Facts` WITH
    `the dog is not sterilised` IS TRUE
    , `the dog's registration was, immediately before the s 16 commencement day, in effect under old s 15` IS TRUE

`s 63 -- a sterilised dog` MEANS `S63 Facts` WITH
    `the dog is not sterilised` IS FALSE
    , `the dog's registration was, immediately before the s 16 commencement day, in effect under old s 15` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 63 -- the pre-2021 s 15 registration regime continues to apply to this registration` `s 63 -- an unsterilised dog registered under old s 15 at commencement`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 63 -- the pre-2021 s 15 registration regime continues to apply to this registration` `s 63 -- a sterilised dog`)

`s 64 -- a pending application at 2021 commencement` MEANS `S64 Facts` WITH
    `application for registration was delivered under s 16(1)` IS TRUE
    , `application was not finally dealt with under s 16(2) before the s 17 commencement day` IS TRUE

`s 64 -- an application already finally dealt with` MEANS `S64 Facts` WITH
    `application for registration was delivered under s 16(1)` IS TRUE
    , `application was not finally dealt with under s 16(2) before the s 17 commencement day` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 64 -- the application is to be dealt with as if s 17(5) had not been enacted` `s 64 -- a pending application at 2021 commencement`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 64 -- the application is to be dealt with as if s 17(5) had not been enacted` `s 64 -- an application already finally dealt with`)

`s 65(2)(a) -- an existing pet shop business before application day` MEANS `S65(2)(a) Facts` WITH
    `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day` IS TRUE
    , `time is before the application day` IS TRUE

`s 65(2)(a) -- the same business, but after application day` MEANS `S65(2)(a) Facts` WITH
    `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day` IS TRUE
    , `time is before the application day` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 65(2)(a) -- ss 38B, 38G, 38H, 38I, 38J, 38K and 38L do not apply to the person's pet shop business or pet shop` `s 65(2)(a) -- an existing pet shop business before application day`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65(2)(a) -- ss 38B, 38G, 38H, 38I, 38J, 38K and 38L do not apply to the person's pet shop business or pet shop` `s 65(2)(a) -- the same business, but after application day`)

`s 65(2)(b) -- a preexisting dog held by an existing pet shop business` MEANS `S65(2)(b) Facts` WITH
    `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day` IS TRUE
    , `the dog is a preexisting dog (supplied to the business before the application day)` IS TRUE

`s 65(2)(b) -- a dog first supplied after application day` MEANS `S65(2)(b) Facts` WITH
    `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day` IS TRUE
    , `the dog is a preexisting dog (supplied to the business before the application day)` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 65(2)(b) -- ss 38G, 38I, 38J, 38K and 38L do not apply to the person in relation to this dog` `s 65(2)(b) -- a preexisting dog held by an existing pet shop business`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65(2)(b) -- ss 38G, 38I, 38J, 38K and 38L do not apply to the person in relation to this dog` `s 65(2)(b) -- a dog first supplied after application day`)

`s 65(3) -- an existing pet shop business before application day` MEANS `S65(3) Facts` WITH
    `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day` IS TRUE
    , `time is before the application day` IS TRUE

`s 65(3) -- the same business, but after application day` MEANS `S65(3) Facts` WITH
    `person conducts a relevant pet shop business immediately before the s 32 commencement day` IS TRUE
    , `time is before the application day` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 65(3) -- s 38N does not apply to the person` `s 65(3) -- an existing pet shop business before application day`
